  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reviewed all 5 patients on \"DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026\" under RBC-PHARM-07. Three ended with a dose change and two ended on their original dose, after records that arrived during the review reversed my first decision for both.\n\n- **pt-0003 Frank Delgado (rivaroxaban): stays on 20 mg daily.** First, the St. Brigid creatinine of 160 µmol/L gave a CrCl of 44, so I lowered the dose to 15 mg (mr-t0001). The lab then sent a corrected result of 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer calibration fault. That gives a CrCl of 60, so I put the dose back to 20 mg (mr-t0007). Notes: doc-t0002 and the correction doc-t0008.\n- **pt-0041 Raymond Duquette (apixaban): lowered from 5 mg to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003).** He is 70, weighs 84 kg and has a creatinine of 0.98, so he meets none of the dose criteria. He is taking itraconazole, which the policy treats as an interacting drug, so the dose drops to 2.5 mg. I left the itraconazole alone. Note: doc-t0004.\n- **pt-0038 Eugene Moravec (rivaroxaban): raised from 15 mg to 20 mg daily (mr-t0005).** He is 79, weighs 96 kg (clinic scale, 10/9) and has a creatinine of 1.45, giving a CrCl of 56. During the review he sent a portal message saying his home scale read 185 lb. The policy doesn't accept patient-reported weights, so the decision stands. Note: doc-t0006; addendum: doc-t0019.\n- **pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino (rivaroxaban): lowered from 20 mg to 15 mg daily (mr-t0010).** A new creatinine of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) came in during the review. At age 75, female, 71 kg, that gives a CrCl of 43.6. The earlier creatinine of 0.92 would have kept her on 20 mg. Note: doc-t0011.\n- **pt-0002 Harold Vance (apixaban): stays on 2.5 mg twice daily.** He meets only the age criterion (82). His weight is 64.9 kg and creatinine 1.21. So I first raised him to 5 mg (mr-t0013). A St. Brigid dermatology letter dated 10/22 then arrived: they started itraconazole 200 mg daily for 12 weeks. That makes the policy dose 2.5 mg, so I changed it back (mr-t0015). Notes: doc-t0014 and the correction doc-t0016.\n\n**Two things to follow up:**\n- **Moravec:** please get a clinic-measured weight at his next visit and repeat the review. At about 84 kg his CrCl would be about 49, which is under the 50 cut-off for the lower dose.\n- **Vance:** please review his apixaban dose again when the itraconazole course ends, around mid-January 2027. On today's numbers he would then go back to 5 mg twice daily.\n\nI didn't change any other medications. I completed the four inbox items that arrived during the review, each linked to the order or note it led to. Older inbox items for patients not on this list were left as they were.",
